    "reference_value": 74.0741025123,
    "public_to_model_scale": 1.0,
    "model_unit": "angstrom^3/conventional_unit_cell"
   },
   "notes": "This is the complete empirical pressure-scale form in Appendix B, not a standalone 300 K Vinet fit. Equation (3) and the three globally optimized coefficients define a zero-temperature cold Vinet curve; Equation (B2) adds an absolute thermal pressure that is nonzero at 300 K. The stored Tr=300 K is the Taylor expansion and operational increment reference, not the temperature of the cold curve. Tables II-III label compression by the ambient initial V0=1/rho0 from rho0=3.590 g/cm^3, whereas Equation (B2) defines eta with the smaller fitted cold V0K. The five new shock states span 152-265 GPa; the three reported temperatures span 3088-5676 K. The full quasi-Debye Helmholtz construction in Equations (1)-(6) is not independently reconstructable from the article because the numerical longitudinal- and shear-velocity versus density fits needed for the Debye-temperature law are not published. The authors therefore supply Equations (B1)-(B2) as the derived executable P-V-T form. No uncertainty confidence level or covariance is reported for the three optimized cold coefficients, and no errors are reported for c0-c5. The APS article record and full paper were checked; no official supplemental file or machine-readable data deposit is linked.",
   "identifier": "mgo_b1_luo_2023_vinet_thermal_5",
   "pressure_calibration": {
    "status": "not_applicable",
    "methods": [
