   "parameter_provenance": {
    "V0": "Fixed in the room-temperature fits to the 74.71(3) A^3 average of prior ambient measurements (discussion preceding Table 3).",
    "K0": "Fixed in the preferred BM3 fit to the adopted acoustic value 161(1) GPa (discussion preceding Table 3).",
    "K0_prime": "Fitted to the combined room-temperature diffraction data: the text gives the formal result as 3.94 +/- 0.06 (Table 3 rounds it to 3.94(5)), and pressure-error propagation expands it to 3.94 +/- 0.2, repeated in the abstract. The conclusion instead prints +/-0.3 without explanation. The explicit propagated +/-0.2 value is stored, and K0' is held fixed in the thermal analysis.",
    "Tr": "The thermal pressure is referenced to the 300 K BM3 isotherm in Section 4.2 and Figure 4.",
    "theta0": "800 +/- 50 K, obtained by fitting the Debye heat-capacity expression to the Anderson and Zou (1989) ambient-pressure thermodynamic data and then adopted in the P-V-T model.",
    "gamma0": "1.45 +/- 0.1, constrained from the zero-pressure thermal-pressure intercept in Section 4.2 and then fixed while q was determined from its pressure dependence.",
    "q": "0.8 +/- 0.5, constrained from the compression dependence of thermal pressure in Section 4.2.",
    "n": "Fixed to two atoms per MgO formula unit in the Debye energy expression."
   },
   "fit_datasets": [
    "mgo_dewaele_2000_table2_pvt"
   ],
   "notes": "Preferred complete P-V-T parameterization from Table 5 and the conclusion: a 300 K third-order Birch-Murnaghan reference isotherm plus quasi-harmonic Mie-Gruneisen-Debye thermal pressure. The implemented theta(V) relation follows exactly from d ln(theta)/d ln(V)=-gamma with gamma=gamma0(V/V0)^q, i.e. the integrated-Gruneisen law. Table 3's Murnaghan, Vinet, logarithmic, and alternate constrained BM3 fits are room-temperature extrapolation comparisons, not separate preferred P-V-T records, and are therefore not added. The static coefficients were obtained from a staged combined-data analysis that included earlier published room-temperature measurements; the bundled Table 2 contains all 61 new observations from this study. The K0' uncertainty is internally inconsistent: formal +/-0.06 in the text (0.05 after Table 3 rounding), pressure-propagated +/-0.2 in the text and abstract, and unexplained +/-0.3 in the conclusion; the stored +/-0.2 follows the explicit error analysis. No official supplement or machine-readable data deposit accompanies the article.",
